  ],
  "next_step": "Close and implement asynchronous Apply preparation using the existing worker and current-owner adoption. First isolate ready/recovery submission, command construction/validation and backend enqueue costs; retain request identity, current authority, full validation and uncertain-result recovery. Keep restore/40 ms adoption/preview work visible and rerun fixed ordinary qualification only after a measured repair.",
  "limitations": [
    "Only direct executable registrations through g_signal_connect_data, g_timeout_add and g_timeout_add_full are observed; toolkit/internal callbacks and scheduling remain uncovered.",
    "Signal marshal guards and timer wrappers perturb execution; callback spans include ordinary marshalling overhead.",
    "Two initial decoder development failures and one cross-clock preflight rejection are preserved. Earlier failed self-test source digests are recorded, but their complete Python source snapshots were not archived. The two campaign attempts have complete source archives.",
    "Product binaries, original case definitions and product code were unchanged. No production admission or full release qualification.",
    "Other signal registration APIs and pre-created closures are unobserved. Timer wrappers preserve source-ID operations but not data-based source lookup; source review found no such lookup in current consumers."
